WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.429 --> 00:00:05.140
Sequels have become such staples in Hollywood
that almost any film will get one if the original

00:00:05.140 --> 00:00:06.229
makes enough money.

00:00:06.229 --> 00:00:10.350
With some movies, however, franchise hopes
are so high in advance that a follow-up is

00:00:10.350 --> 00:00:14.610
already being put in motion long before the
flick ever hits theaters … which makes the

00:00:14.610 --> 00:00:17.360
fall that much harder if and when it flops.

00:00:17.360 --> 00:00:22.170
Here are some sequels that never happened
because their predecessor pics were so poor.

00:00:22.170 --> 00:00:23.400
Independence Day 3

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:28.410
It took 20 years for Independence Day to get
its first sequel, but Independence Day: Resurgence

00:00:28.410 --> 00:00:32.840
was expected to be the first of three planned
follow-up films that would continue Roland

00:00:32.840 --> 00:00:34.790
Emmerich's alien invasion story.

00:00:34.790 --> 00:00:38.940
The original movie was a box office smash
and earned mostly favorable reviews.

00:00:38.940 --> 00:00:43.180
But Resurgence turned out to be too little,
too late to resurrect that moment.

00:00:43.180 --> 00:00:47.480
The movie was slammed by critics for being
an elaborate but ultimately empty spectacle.

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:51.970
And while it wasn't an intergalactic bomb
at the ticket booth, its lackluster receipts

00:00:51.970 --> 00:00:56.690
didn't indicate much audience interest in
the movie or its potential sequels, either.

00:00:56.690 --> 00:01:01.260
Eventually, those ambitious franchise plans
seemed to fizzle in the wake of its release.

00:01:01.260 --> 00:01:03.969
Maybe they shouldn't have killed off Captain
Hiller after all.

00:01:03.969 --> 00:01:05.119
"That's right!

00:01:05.119 --> 00:01:06.280
That's right!"

00:01:06.280 --> 00:01:09.530
There's still some hope for those who'd like
to see the future of the series, which would

00:01:09.530 --> 00:01:12.270
see some of its heroes on a new space adventure.

00:01:12.270 --> 00:01:16.320
According to Emmerich, he and the studio are
considering turning to the small screen to

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:18.660
carry out the next Independence Day adventure.

00:01:18.660 --> 00:01:19.780
Who knows?

00:01:19.780 --> 00:01:23.590
Maybe those crazy aliens will find a welcome
new home on the small screen.

00:01:23.590 --> 00:01:24.799
Battleship 2

00:01:24.799 --> 00:01:27.340
Hopes were very high for Battleship.

00:01:27.340 --> 00:01:31.970
So high, in fact, that Universal Pictures
signed a six year deal with Hasbro Games,

00:01:31.970 --> 00:01:37.340
makers of family favorites like Clue and Candyland,
so that they could become the de facto board-game-to-cinema

00:01:37.340 --> 00:01:38.340
provider.

00:01:38.340 --> 00:01:43.299
However, it's first big attempt was a $220
million wash for the studio, as Battleship

00:01:43.299 --> 00:01:46.530
decidedly sunk with critics and audiences
alike.

00:01:46.530 --> 00:01:51.600
Director Peter Berg placed the blame on stiff
competition, in particular Marvel's The Avengers.

00:01:51.600 --> 00:01:55.860
But the fact that it was derided for drowning
all plot potential in a sea of formulaic action

00:01:55.860 --> 00:01:59.630
sequences didn't convince audiences to hop
aboard the ride either.

00:01:59.630 --> 00:02:00.970
"Negative, sir, it's a miss."

00:02:00.970 --> 00:02:05.590
Battleship was set up to be a studio tentpole,
but after it was torpedoed with bad reviews

00:02:05.590 --> 00:02:10.439
and dismal ticket sales, Universal quietly
scuppered those plans — and several other

00:02:10.439 --> 00:02:14.459
Hasbro-based pics they'd been banking on have
failed to set sail as well.

00:02:14.459 --> 00:02:18.659
Maybe someone should've foreseen that a boat
movie by a guy named Berg might not work out

00:02:18.660 --> 00:02:19.380
so well.

00:02:19.380 --> 00:02:19.900
"Iceberg!

00:02:19.900 --> 00:02:20.400
Right ahead!"

00:02:24.280 --> 00:02:26.980
Divergent: Ascendant

00:02:26.999 --> 00:02:30.889
Even the Veronica Roth faithful were turned
off by the third installment of the Divergent

00:02:30.889 --> 00:02:31.919
book series.

00:02:31.919 --> 00:02:35.799
The trilogy's finale received grimmer reviews
than its predecessors from readers who were

00:02:35.799 --> 00:02:38.019
disappointed at its hectic conclusion.

00:02:38.019 --> 00:02:42.370
So when Lionsgate announced they'd be dividing
the final adaptation installment into two

00:02:42.370 --> 00:02:46.230
films, the collective eye-rolling among Divergent
fans was intense.

00:02:46.230 --> 00:02:50.290
The first two Divergent installments weren't
built for critics, so it didn't matter that

00:02:50.290 --> 00:02:52.439
they weren't lapped with praise or prestige.

00:02:52.439 --> 00:02:55.959
They still earned enough money to justify
carrying on with the franchise.

00:02:55.959 --> 00:03:00.790
However, the third film was an unmitigated
disaster on all fronts, earning laughingstock

00:03:00.790 --> 00:03:05.599
status with critics and barely bringing in
half of what Insurgent did at the box office.

00:03:05.599 --> 00:03:09.870
The production budget on the would-be final
installment, Ascendant, was immediately slashed,

00:03:09.870 --> 00:03:12.200
and that was just the start of its trouble.

00:03:12.200 --> 00:03:16.371
The director soon diverged from the project,
and after the studio revealed they'd turn

00:03:16.371 --> 00:03:20.389
to television to produce the final chapter,
several cast members hopped off the train

00:03:20.389 --> 00:03:21.389
as well.

00:03:21.389 --> 00:03:25.719
Whether it's dystopia fatigue or simple dislike
of the source material that caused audiences

00:03:25.719 --> 00:03:30.839
to tune out, the franchise seemed to be lost
before it could arrive at its final destination.

00:03:30.839 --> 00:03:35.169
Several months after its originally slated
release date for Ascendant passed by, however,

00:03:35.169 --> 00:03:39.639
Lionsgate announced a new plan to develop
Divergent's final leg as a TV series on the

00:03:39.639 --> 00:03:40.709
Starz network.

00:03:40.709 --> 00:03:45.609
But without its original initiates onboard
to finish the futuristic saga, it hardly qualifies

00:03:45.609 --> 00:03:47.219
as a true sequel.

00:03:47.219 --> 00:03:48.749
Jumper 2

00:03:48.749 --> 00:03:53.260
Based on the Steven Gould novels, Jumper was
a sci-fi extravaganza that was clearly supposed

00:03:53.260 --> 00:03:54.260
to do more.

00:03:54.260 --> 00:03:58.420
With a promising young cast, an open ending,
and a frenetic story that could easily be

00:03:58.420 --> 00:04:02.459
continued in new adventures, it had "franchise
hopeful" written all over it.

00:04:02.459 --> 00:04:06.999
Despite a tepid box office take and terrible
reviews, lead actor Hayden Christensen claimed

00:04:06.999 --> 00:04:11.729
sequel plans were still in development with
the studio even two years after the original's

00:04:11.729 --> 00:04:12.729
release.

00:04:12.729 --> 00:04:15.519
According to him, the sequel would've followed
its heroes to a darker place.

00:04:15.519 --> 00:04:20.329
Leap forward a decade, though, and 20th Century
Fox is officially out of the Jumper movie

00:04:20.329 --> 00:04:21.329
business.

00:04:21.329 --> 00:04:26.919
Director Doug Liman has since managed to transport
the property to another locale for a reboot-slash-sequel

00:04:26.919 --> 00:04:28.330
produced by YouTube Red.

00:04:28.330 --> 00:04:32.669
However, instead of continuing on with Christensen's
character's journey based on the second book

00:04:32.669 --> 00:04:37.240
Reflex, the new series will be adapted from
the third novel in the series, Impulse.

00:04:37.240 --> 00:04:40.810
This installment focuses on his eventual daughter
instead of him.

00:04:40.810 --> 00:04:45.280
Meanwhile, actor Jamie Bell has taken it upon
himself to start up another small screen reboot

00:04:45.280 --> 00:04:49.470
based on the property, which may or may not
feature him in his original role from the

00:04:49.470 --> 00:04:50.460
2008 film.

00:04:51.660 --> 00:04:53.379
"Did you think you were the only one?"

00:04:53.379 --> 00:04:57.730
So while Jumper might have built a launchpad
for separate projects, whatever launch plans

00:04:57.730 --> 00:05:01.300
they had for Jumper 2 have obviously failed
to clear the hurdle.

00:05:01.300 --> 00:05:03.110
The Power of Six

00:05:03.110 --> 00:05:07.770
The Pittacus Lore novel series, upon which
I Am Number Four was based, was wildly popular

00:05:07.770 --> 00:05:09.240
when the first film dropped.

00:05:09.240 --> 00:05:13.780
And in an era when Young Adult adaptations
were all the rage and actor Alex Pettyfer

00:05:13.780 --> 00:05:17.979
was considered the up-and-coming heartthrob,
the film was expected to launch a full-on

00:05:17.979 --> 00:05:19.780
franchise for DreamWorks.

00:05:19.780 --> 00:05:24.430
The sci-fi adventure told the story of powerful
alien teens who are being hunted into extinction,

00:05:24.430 --> 00:05:28.570
and would've been followed up with Teresa
Palmer leading The Power of Six.

00:05:28.570 --> 00:05:33.199
But after the first film drew the ire of critics
and the disinterest of audiences, the sequel

00:05:33.199 --> 00:05:34.909
was ultimately shelved.

00:05:34.909 --> 00:05:39.449
Screenwriter Marti Noxon told Collider that
result was regrettable because "Number 6 was

00:05:39.449 --> 00:05:42.330
really awesome and I would have liked to have
seen a lot more of her.

00:05:42.330 --> 00:05:44.100
We need another kick-ass girl heroine."

00:05:44.100 --> 00:05:47.960
Considering how underwhelming Four turned
out to be, maybe they should've just skipped

00:05:47.960 --> 00:05:51.129
ahead to the next number in the first place.

00:05:51.129 --> 00:05:52.289
Showgirls 2

00:05:52.289 --> 00:05:56.090
Given Showgirls' continued status as one of
the most widely derided movies of all time,

00:05:56.090 --> 00:05:59.099
it may be hard to believe there could've ever
been a sequel.

00:05:59.099 --> 00:06:03.630
According to director Paul Verhoeven, however,
Elizabeth Berkley was supposed to take another

00:06:03.630 --> 00:06:08.479
turn on the stripper pole — before the movie's
terrible reception left her career in tatters.

00:06:08.479 --> 00:06:12.800
He told movie site JoBlo, "we had actually
been working on the sequel to Showgirls which

00:06:12.800 --> 00:06:17.200
was going to be called Bimbos and was going
to be 'Nomi does Hollywood,' but after Showgirls

00:06:17.200 --> 00:06:20.699
was released there was no way anyone was going
to give me the money for that.

00:06:20.699 --> 00:06:25.120
If we could just make Elizabeth Berkley 20
years younger now I would love to make Bimbos

00:06:25.120 --> 00:06:26.120
today."

00:06:26.120 --> 00:06:29.749
Considering how she seemed to time-travel
right back to high school for that mini-Saved

00:06:29.749 --> 00:06:34.800
By the Bell reunion in 2015, it's probably
not her age that'll keep Bimbos from ever

00:06:34.800 --> 00:06:35.540
happening.

00:06:35.540 --> 00:06:36.540
Thanks for watching!

00:06:36.800 --> 00:06:39.139
